{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to checker approval a8031cba of S3. Its Security section says that a member \"can no longer exhaust the type for good\". That is too strong. The repair ends accidental stranding, because a requester can now always close their own request. A member holding `issue.comment` who opens 64 requests and never withdraws them can still fill `approval-request` in that issue, and only that member's own withdrawal frees them. This fails closed and doesn't touch authority. It's the same kind of limit as the per-member note limit that ruling f4495460 places with BO3, so it doesn't block this head. The planner may want to carry it to the same place.\n\nThe verdict doesn't change.","body":{"to":"planner"}}